window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b136-3109c222f408cb69.json"]={sha256:"3109c222f408cb69ea902316dc478a9b0a1636466eca462afcb50b02c38b3708",value:{"id":"b136","title":"土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良","titleEn":"Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦用流變、含水與體積收支評估土壓平衡潛盾改良土的功能。沿著調查依據、物理作用、數量估算、現場驗證到工程交接逐項建立可追溯的推論鏈，特別辨別單一數值無法揭露的空間差異及時間效應。以獨立量測檢驗簡化模型，並把觀測結果、教學假設與需要主管工程師審查的決策清楚分列。","summaryEn":"This course focuses on assess EPB conditioned-ground function through rheology, moisture and volume accounting. It develops a traceable reasoning chain from evidence and physical processes through quantitative estimates, field verification and engineering handover. Spatial variation and time effects are separated from a single nominal result. Independent observations test the simplified models, while measured evidence, teaching assumptions and decisions requiring the responsible engineer remain explicitly distinguished.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-tbm","subcategoryTitle":"潛盾與掘進系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Shield and tunnel-boring systems","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-tbm","learningTags":["underground","ug-tbm","tbm"],"architectureFamily":"tbm","architectureNodes":[["塑性土塞的功能","Function of the plastic soil plug"],["泡沫體積與壓縮","Foam volume and compression"],["流變屈服與黏度","Yield stress and viscosity"],["添加收支與混合均勻","Addition balance and mixing uniformity"],["改良試驗到現場移交","Conditioning trials and field handover"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[3,1]],"diagram":{"type":"tbm","labels":["塑性土塞的功能","泡沫體積與壓縮","流變屈服與黏度","添加收支與混合均勻","改良試驗到現場移交"],"labelsEn":["Function of the plastic soil plug","Foam volume and compression","Yield stress and viscosity","Addition balance and mixing uniformity","Conditioning trials and field handover"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創教學算例，所有輸入是為比較機制而假設，並非任何地標的實測資料。以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設螺旋機長8 m、兩端壓差160 kPa，平均梯度20 kPa/m；僅描述量測，不是允許設定。以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設乾土1000 kg、水250 kg，w=25%；水占濕土1250 kg的比例為20%，兩者不可混用。將第一式的一個線性乘數加倍而固定其他邊界，該項貢獻隨之加倍；若為非線性式則必須重新代入，不能等比例外推。把輸入值、單位換算、計算結果及假設列成四欄，再用獨立計算器重算；最後比較量測誤差與模型簡化，判斷改變是否足以支持工程決策。","textEn":"Original teaching example: all inputs are assumptions for comparing mechanisms, not measurements from a landmark project. The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume an 8 m screw with a 160 kPa end-to-end pressure difference; the mean gradient is 20 kPa/m, describing a measurement rather than an operating setting. The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume dry soil 1000 kg and water 250 kg; moisture content is 25%, while water is 20% of the 1250 kg wet mass. Doubling one linear multiplicative input in the first relation while holding the remaining boundaries fixed doubles that contribution; a nonlinear relation must instead be evaluated again. Tabulate inputs, unit conversions, results and assumptions in separate columns, and recalculate independently. Finally compare measurement uncertainty with model simplification before deciding whether the difference supports an engineering decision.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b136-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「塑性土塞的功能」與「含水率基準轉換」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Function of the plastic soil plug\" and \"Moisture-basis conversion\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b136-v14-01","title":"塑性土塞的功能：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Function of the plastic soil plug: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「塑性土塞的功能」如何影響土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Function of the plastic soil plug” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"土壓平衡依靠倉內改良土傳遞支護並容許受控出土，材料同時需要可塑性與低滲透。過乾會難以攪拌，過稀則難形成壓降，因此不能把流動性越高當成越好的改良。 假設螺旋機長8 m、兩端壓差160 kPa，平均梯度20 kPa/m；僅描述量測，不是允許設定。 過度液化可能出現壓力快速流失，乾硬土團則造成間歇堵塞和扭矩跳升；兩種相反狀態都可能以平均出土量正常掩蓋，需看時間歷程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「塑性土塞的功能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"EPB chamber material must transmit support while permitting controlled extraction, requiring plasticity and limited permeability together. Dry material resists mixing while overly fluid material may not sustain a pressure drop, so maximum flowability is not the objective. Assume an 8 m screw with a 160 kPa end-to-end pressure difference; the mean gradient is 20 kPa/m, describing a measurement rather than an operating setting. Overfluid material can lose pressure rapidly, while stiff lumps cause intermittent blockage and torque spikes. Both can hide behind a normal average discharge, requiring time-resolved interpretation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Function of the plastic soil plug” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「改良土越稀越容易流動，就一定越有利於穩定支護。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More fluid conditioned soil is necessarily better for stable face support.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「塑性土塞的功能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Function of the plastic soil plug”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-01-k1","title":"塑性土塞的功能","titleEn":"Function of the plastic soil plug","text":"土壓平衡依靠倉內改良土傳遞支護並容許受控出土，材料同時需要可塑性與低滲透。過乾會難以攪拌，過稀則難形成壓降，因此不能把流動性越高當成越好的改良。","textEn":"EPB chamber material must transmit support while permitting controlled extraction, requiring plasticity and limited permeability together. Dry material resists mixing while overly fluid material may not sustain a pressure drop, so maximum flowability is not the objective.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：改良土越稀越容易流動，就一定越有利於穩定支護。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More fluid conditioned soil is necessarily better for stable face support. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「塑性土塞的功能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Function of the plastic soil plug\" is correct?","options":["改良土越稀越容易流動，就一定越有利於穩定支護。","土壓平衡依靠倉內改良土傳遞支護並容許受控出土，材料同時需要可塑性與低滲透。","乾基含水率與水占濕土重量比例永遠可以互換。"],"optionsEn":["More fluid conditioned soil is necessarily better for stable face support.","EPB chamber material must transmit support while permitting controlled extraction, requiring plasticity and limited permeability together.","Dry-basis moisture content and water fraction of wet mass are always interchangeable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"土壓平衡依靠倉內改良土傳遞支護並容許受控出土，材料同時需要可塑性與低滲透。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"EPB chamber material must transmit support while permitting controlled extraction, requiring plasticity and limited permeability together. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b136-v14-02","title":"塑性土塞的功能：定量估算","titleEn":"Function of the plastic soil plug: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「塑性土塞的功能」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Function of the plastic soil plug” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設螺旋機長8 m、兩端壓差160 kPa，平均梯度20 kPa/m；僅描述量測，不是允許設定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume an 8 m screw with a 160 kPa end-to-end pressure difference; the mean gradient is 20 kPa/m, describing a measurement rather than an operating setting. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將代表性土樣的流動性、滲透與螺旋機壓力分布一起比較，記錄含水及粒徑；只有可維持壓力傳遞且出土穩定的試驗組合才供工程審查，不能靠單一坍度值認定合格。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare workability and permeability of representative samples with screw pressure distribution, recording moisture and grading; engineering review needs stable pressure transmission and extraction rather than acceptance from slump alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設螺旋機長8 m、兩端壓差160 kPa，平均梯度20 kPa/m；僅描述量測，不是允許設定。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume an 8 m screw with a 160 kPa end-to-end pressure difference; the mean gradient is 20 kPa/m, describing a measurement rather than an operating setting.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「塑性土塞的功能」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Function of the plastic soil plug\", which statement holds?","options":["細料百分比相同的土一定具有相同塑性和改良需求。","刀盤功率降低就能證明改良成功，不必看進尺和地質。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Soils with equal fines content necessarily have equal plasticity and conditioning needs.","Lower cutterhead power proves successful conditioning without checking advance or geology.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b136-v14-03","title":"塑性土塞的功能：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Function of the plastic soil plug: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「塑性土塞的功能」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Function of the plastic soil plug” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將代表性土樣的流動性、滲透與螺旋機壓力分布一起比較，記錄含水及粒徑；只有可維持壓力傳遞且出土穩定的試驗組合才供工程審查，不能靠單一坍度值認定合格。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：過度液化可能出現壓力快速流失，乾硬土團則造成間歇堵塞和扭矩跳升；兩種相反狀態都可能以平均出土量正常掩蓋，需看時間歷程。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare workability and permeability of representative samples with screw pressure distribution, recording moisture and grading; engineering review needs stable pressure transmission and extraction rather than acceptance from slump alone. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Overfluid material can lose pressure rapidly, while stiff lumps cause intermittent blockage and torque spikes. Both can hide behind a normal average discharge, requiring time-resolved interpretation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄塑性土塞的功能的資料來源與適用條件。將代表性土樣的流動性、滲透與螺旋機壓力分布一起比較，記錄含水及粒徑；只有可維持壓力傳遞且出土穩定的試驗組合才供工程審查，不能靠單一坍度值認定合格。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for function of the plastic soil plug. Compare workability and permeability of representative samples with screw pressure distribution, recording moisture and grading; engineering review needs stable pressure transmission and extraction rather than acceptance from slump alone.","failure":"注意干擾：過度液化可能出現壓力快速流失，乾硬土團則造成間歇堵塞和扭矩跳升；兩種相反狀態都可能以平均出土量正常掩蓋，需看時間歷程。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Overfluid material can lose pressure rapidly, while stiff lumps cause intermittent blockage and torque spikes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將代表性土樣的流動性、滲透與螺旋機壓力分布一起比較，記錄含水及粒徑；只有可維持壓力傳遞且出土穩定的試驗組合才供工程審查，不能靠單一坍度值認定合格。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：過度液化可能出現壓力快速流失，乾硬土團則造成間歇堵塞和扭矩跳升；兩種相反狀態都可能以平均出土量正常掩蓋，需看時間歷程。","textEn":"Compare workability and permeability of representative samples with screw pressure distribution, recording moisture and grading; engineering review needs stable pressure transmission and extraction rather than acceptance from slump alone. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Overfluid material can lose pressure rapidly, while stiff lumps cause intermittent blockage and torque spikes. Both can hide behind a normal average discharge, requiring time-resolved interpretation.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄塑性土塞的功能的資料來源與適用條件。將代表性土樣的流動性、滲透與螺旋機壓力分布一起比較，記錄含水及粒徑；只有可維持壓力傳遞且出土穩定的試驗組合才供工程審查，不能靠單一坍度值認定合格。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for function of the plastic soil plug. Compare workability and permeability of representative samples with screw pressure distribution, recording moisture and grading; engineering review needs stable pressure transmission and extraction rather than acceptance from slump alone.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「塑性土塞的功能」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Function of the plastic soil plug\"?","options":["將代表性土樣的流動性、滲透與螺旋機壓力分布一起比較，記錄含水及粒徑；只有可維持壓力傳遞且出土穩定的試驗組合才供工程審查，不能靠單一坍度值認定合格。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","試驗流量測不到就證明改良土真正完全不透水。"],"optionsEn":["Compare workability and permeability of representative samples with screw pressure distribution, recording moisture and grading.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Undetectable test flow proves that conditioned soil has exactly zero permeability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將代表性土樣的流動性、滲透與螺旋機壓力分布一起比較，記錄含水及粒徑；只有可維持壓力傳遞且出土穩定的試驗組合才供工程審查，不能靠單一坍度值認定合格。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare workability and permeability of representative samples with screw pressure distribution, recording moisture and grading; engineering review needs stable pressure transmission and extraction rather than acceptance from slump alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b136-v14-04","title":"塑性土塞的功能：失效診斷","titleEn":"Function of the plastic soil plug: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「塑性土塞的功能」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Function of the plastic soil plug” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"過度液化可能出現壓力快速流失，乾硬土團則造成間歇堵塞和扭矩跳升；兩種相反狀態都可能以平均出土量正常掩蓋，需看時間歷程。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Overfluid material can lose pressure rapidly, while stiff lumps cause intermittent blockage and torque spikes. Both can hide behind a normal average discharge, requiring time-resolved interpretation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：過度液化可能出現壓力快速流失，乾硬土團則造成間歇堵塞和扭矩跳升；兩種相反狀態都可能以平均出土量正常掩蓋，需看時間歷程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Both can hide behind a normal average discharge, requiring time-resolved interpretation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「改良土越稀越容易流動，就一定越有利於穩定支護。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More fluid conditioned soil is necessarily better for stable face support.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"過度液化可能出現壓力快速流失，乾硬土團則造成間歇堵塞和扭矩跳升；兩種相反狀態都可能以平均出土量正常掩蓋，需看時間歷程。","textEn":"Overfluid material can lose pressure rapidly, while stiff lumps cause intermittent blockage and torque spikes. Both can hide behind a normal average discharge, requiring time-resolved interpretation.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「塑性土塞的功能」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Function of the plastic soil plug\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","過度液化可能出現壓力快速流失，乾硬土團則造成間歇堵塞和扭矩跳升；兩種相反狀態都可能以平均出土量正常掩蓋，需看時間歷程。","乾基含水率與水占濕土重量比例永遠可以互換。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Overfluid material can lose pressure rapidly, while stiff lumps cause intermittent blockage and torque spikes.","Dry-basis moisture content and water fraction of wet mass are always interchangeable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"過度液化可能出現壓力快速流失，乾硬土團則造成間歇堵塞和扭矩跳升；兩種相反狀態都可能以平均出土量正常掩蓋，需看時間歷程。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Overfluid material can lose pressure rapidly, while stiff lumps cause intermittent blockage and torque spikes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b136-v14-05","title":"含水率基準轉換：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Moisture-basis conversion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「含水率基準轉換」如何影響土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Moisture-basis conversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"土壤含水率通常以水重除乾土重，與水占濕土總重比例不同。改良效果與黏土礦物及原水量有關，必須先統一質量基準再比較添加量，否則看似相同百分比其實不是同一材料。 假設乾土1000 kg、水250 kg，w=25%；水占濕土1250 kg的比例為20%，兩者不可混用。 把濕基百分比當乾基會錯估改良水量，倉內土與皮帶土失水程度不同又造成比較偏差；誤差可能被錯怪為添加劑性能不穩定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「含水率基準轉換」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Geotechnical moisture content divides water mass by dry soil mass, unlike wet-mass fraction. Conditioning depends on mineralogy and initial water, requiring a consistent mass basis before comparing addition percentages or material behavior. Assume dry soil 1000 kg and water 250 kg; moisture content is 25%, while water is 20% of the 1250 kg wet mass. Confusing wet and dry bases misstates conditioning water, while chamber and belt samples may lose different amounts. The resulting inconsistency can be wrongly attributed to unstable additive performance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Moisture-basis conversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「乾基含水率與水占濕土重量比例永遠可以互換。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dry-basis moisture content and water fraction of wet mass are always interchangeable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「含水率基準轉換」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Moisture-basis conversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-05-k1","title":"含水率基準轉換","titleEn":"Moisture-basis conversion","text":"土壤含水率通常以水重除乾土重，與水占濕土總重比例不同。改良效果與黏土礦物及原水量有關，必須先統一質量基準再比較添加量，否則看似相同百分比其實不是同一材料。","textEn":"Geotechnical moisture content divides water mass by dry soil mass, unlike wet-mass fraction. Conditioning depends on mineralogy and initial water, requiring a consistent mass basis before comparing addition percentages or material behavior.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：乾基含水率與水占濕土重量比例永遠可以互換。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dry-basis moisture content and water fraction of wet mass are always interchangeable. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「含水率基準轉換」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Moisture-basis conversion\" is correct?","options":["乾基含水率與水占濕土重量比例永遠可以互換。","常壓泡沫體積就是進入加壓土倉後的有效氣體體積。","土壤含水率通常以水重除乾土重，與水占濕土總重比例不同。"],"optionsEn":["Dry-basis moisture content and water fraction of wet mass are always interchangeable.","Atmospheric foam volume equals its effective gas volume inside the pressurized chamber.","Geotechnical moisture content divides water mass by dry soil mass, unlike wet-mass fraction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"土壤含水率通常以水重除乾土重，與水占濕土總重比例不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Geotechnical moisture content divides water mass by dry soil mass, unlike wet-mass fraction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b136-v14-06","title":"含水率基準轉換：定量估算","titleEn":"Moisture-basis conversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「含水率基準轉換」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Moisture-basis conversion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設乾土1000 kg、水250 kg，w=25%；水占濕土1250 kg的比例為20%，兩者不可混用。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume dry soil 1000 kg and water 250 kg; moisture content is 25%, while water is 20% of the 1250 kg wet mass. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以烘乾或適用快速方法核對水量，將原土含水、加水和其他液體分欄；抽樣位置與時間需對齊出土資料，設計者只有在基準和代表性清楚後才比較不同配比試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check water using drying or an appropriate rapid method and separate original moisture, added water and other liquids; align sampling location and time with discharge before designers compare trial mixtures on a common representative basis.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設乾土1000 kg、水250 kg，w=25%；水占濕土1250 kg的比例為20%，兩者不可混用。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume dry soil 1000 kg and water 250 kg; moisture content is 25%, while water is 20% of the 1250 kg wet mass.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「含水率基準轉換」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Moisture-basis conversion\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","單一剪切速率的黏度足以代表停放和重啟流變行為。","添加總量達標就證明各區材料分布一定均勻。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Viscosity at one shear rate fully represents rest and restart rheology.","Meeting the total addition quantity proves uniform distribution throughout the chamber."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b136-v14-07","title":"含水率基準轉換：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Moisture-basis conversion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「含水率基準轉換」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Moisture-basis conversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以烘乾或適用快速方法核對水量，將原土含水、加水和其他液體分欄；抽樣位置與時間需對齊出土資料，設計者只有在基準和代表性清楚後才比較不同配比試驗。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把濕基百分比當乾基會錯估改良水量，倉內土與皮帶土失水程度不同又造成比較偏差；誤差可能被錯怪為添加劑性能不穩定。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check water using drying or an appropriate rapid method and separate original moisture, added water and other liquids; align sampling location and time with discharge before designers compare trial mixtures on a common representative basis. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Confusing wet and dry bases misstates conditioning water, while chamber and belt samples may lose different amounts. The resulting inconsistency can be wrongly attributed to unstable additive performance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄含水率基準轉換的資料來源與適用條件。以烘乾或適用快速方法核對水量，將原土含水、加水和其他液體分欄；抽樣位置與時間需對齊出土資料，設計者只有在基準和代表性清楚後才比較不同配比試驗。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for moisture-basis conversion. Check water using drying or an appropriate rapid method and separate original moisture, added water and other liquids; align sampling location and time with discharge before designers compare trial mixtures on a common representative basis.","failure":"注意干擾：把濕基百分比當乾基會錯估改良水量，倉內土與皮帶土失水程度不同又造成比較偏差；誤差可能被錯怪為添加劑性能不穩定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing wet and dry bases misstates conditioning water, while chamber and belt samples may lose different amounts. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以烘乾或適用快速方法核對水量，將原土含水、加水和其他液體分欄；抽樣位置與時間需對齊出土資料，設計者只有在基準和代表性清楚後才比較不同配比試驗。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把濕基百分比當乾基會錯估改良水量，倉內土與皮帶土失水程度不同又造成比較偏差；誤差可能被錯怪為添加劑性能不穩定。","textEn":"Check water using drying or an appropriate rapid method and separate original moisture, added water and other liquids; align sampling location and time with discharge before designers compare trial mixtures on a common representative basis. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Confusing wet and dry bases misstates conditioning water, while chamber and belt samples may lose different amounts. The resulting inconsistency can be wrongly attributed to unstable additive performance.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄含水率基準轉換的資料來源與適用條件。以烘乾或適用快速方法核對水量，將原土含水、加水和其他液體分欄；抽樣位置與時間需對齊出土資料，設計者只有在基準和代表性清楚後才比較不同配比試驗。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for moisture-basis conversion. Check water using drying or an appropriate rapid method and separate original moisture, added water and other liquids; align sampling location and time with discharge before designers compare trial mixtures on a common representative basis.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「含水率基準轉換」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Moisture-basis conversion\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以烘乾或適用快速方法核對水量，將原土含水、加水和其他液體分欄；抽樣位置與時間需對齊出土資料，設計者只有在基準和代表性清楚後才比較不同配比試驗。","材料短時試驗合格就保證任何溫度和停放時間都相容。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Check water using drying or an appropriate rapid method and separate original moisture, added water and other liquids.","Passing a short trial guarantees compatibility at every temperature and storage duration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以烘乾或適用快速方法核對水量，將原土含水、加水和其他液體分欄；抽樣位置與時間需對齊出土資料，設計者只有在基準和代表性清楚後才比較不同配比試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check water using drying or an appropriate rapid method and separate original moisture, added water and other liquids; align sampling location and time with discharge before designers compare trial mixtures on a common representative basis. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b136-v14-08","title":"含水率基準轉換：失效診斷","titleEn":"Moisture-basis conversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「含水率基準轉換」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Moisture-basis conversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把濕基百分比當乾基會錯估改良水量，倉內土與皮帶土失水程度不同又造成比較偏差；誤差可能被錯怪為添加劑性能不穩定。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing wet and dry bases misstates conditioning water, while chamber and belt samples may lose different amounts. The resulting inconsistency can be wrongly attributed to unstable additive performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把濕基百分比當乾基會錯估改良水量，倉內土與皮帶土失水程度不同又造成比較偏差；誤差可能被錯怪為添加劑性能不穩定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The resulting inconsistency can be wrongly attributed to unstable additive performance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「乾基含水率與水占濕土重量比例永遠可以互換。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dry-basis moisture content and water fraction of wet mass are always interchangeable.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把濕基百分比當乾基會錯估改良水量，倉內土與皮帶土失水程度不同又造成比較偏差；誤差可能被錯怪為添加劑性能不穩定。","textEn":"Confusing wet and dry bases misstates conditioning water, while chamber and belt samples may lose different amounts. The resulting inconsistency can be wrongly attributed to unstable additive performance.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「含水率基準轉換」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Moisture-basis conversion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","常壓泡沫體積就是進入加壓土倉後的有效氣體體積。","把濕基百分比當乾基會錯估改良水量，倉內土與皮帶土失水程度不同又造成比較偏差；誤差可能被錯怪為添加劑性能不穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Atmospheric foam volume equals its effective gas volume inside the pressurized chamber.","Confusing wet and dry bases misstates conditioning water, while chamber and belt samples may lose different amounts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把濕基百分比當乾基會錯估改良水量，倉內土與皮帶土失水程度不同又造成比較偏差；誤差可能被錯怪為添加劑性能不穩定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing wet and dry bases misstates conditioning water, while chamber and belt samples may lose different amounts. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b136-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「泡沫體積與壓縮」與「粒徑與細料作用」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Foam volume and compression\" and \"Grading and fines behavior\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b136-v14-09","title":"泡沫體積與壓縮：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Foam volume and compression: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「泡沫體積與壓縮」如何影響土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Foam volume and compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"泡沫含大量可壓縮氣體，地面量測體積進入加壓土倉後會縮小，故體積比需說明壓力基準。氣泡穩定性和土粒吸附另會改變時間行為，理想氣體換算只提供第一層量級檢查。 假設等溫理想氣體由絕對壓100增至300 kPa，初始氣體3 m³縮至1 m³；液相體積未計。 使用表壓代替絕對壓會造成嚴重壓縮換算錯誤，忽略破泡又會高估可用氣泡；控制系統以錯誤體積基準比較時可能誤判材料不足或過量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「泡沫體積與壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Foam contains compressible gas, so atmospheric volume shrinks in a pressurized chamber and every volumetric ratio needs a pressure reference. Stability and particle interaction add time effects beyond a first-order ideal-gas check. Assume isothermal ideal gas compressed from absolute 100 to 300 kPa; 3 m³ becomes 1 m³, excluding liquid volume. Using gauge instead of absolute pressure corrupts compression calculations, while ignored collapse overstates available bubbles. A control comparison on the wrong volume basis can falsely indicate shortage or excess conditioning. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Foam volume and compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「常壓泡沫體積就是進入加壓土倉後的有效氣體體積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Atmospheric foam volume equals its effective gas volume inside the pressurized chamber.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「泡沫體積與壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Foam volume and compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-09-k1","title":"泡沫體積與壓縮","titleEn":"Foam volume and compression","text":"泡沫含大量可壓縮氣體，地面量測體積進入加壓土倉後會縮小，故體積比需說明壓力基準。氣泡穩定性和土粒吸附另會改變時間行為，理想氣體換算只提供第一層量級檢查。","textEn":"Foam contains compressible gas, so atmospheric volume shrinks in a pressurized chamber and every volumetric ratio needs a pressure reference. Stability and particle interaction add time effects beyond a first-order ideal-gas check.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：常壓泡沫體積就是進入加壓土倉後的有效氣體體積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Atmospheric foam volume equals its effective gas volume inside the pressurized chamber. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「泡沫體積與壓縮」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Foam volume and compression\" is correct?","options":["泡沫含大量可壓縮氣體，地面量測體積進入加壓土倉後會縮小，故體積比需說明壓力基準。","常壓泡沫體積就是進入加壓土倉後的有效氣體體積。","細料百分比相同的土一定具有相同塑性和改良需求。"],"optionsEn":["Foam contains compressible gas, so atmospheric volume shrinks in a pressurized chamber and every volumetric ratio needs a pressure reference.","Atmospheric foam volume equals its effective gas volume inside the pressurized chamber.","Soils with equal fines content necessarily have equal plasticity and conditioning needs."],"answer":0,"explanation":"泡沫含大量可壓縮氣體，地面量測體積進入加壓土倉後會縮小，故體積比需說明壓力基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Foam contains compressible gas, so atmospheric volume shrinks in a pressurized chamber and every volumetric ratio needs a pressure reference. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b136-v14-10","title":"泡沫體積與壓縮：定量估算","titleEn":"Foam volume and compression: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「泡沫體積與壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Foam volume and compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設等溫理想氣體由絕對壓100增至300 kPa，初始氣體3 m³縮至1 m³；液相體積未計。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume isothermal ideal gas compressed from absolute 100 to 300 kPa; 3 m³ becomes 1 m³, excluding liquid volume. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對流量計量測位置、壓力種類及泡沫氣液比例，使用合格試驗觀察加壓後的穩定性；所有體積比附標準狀態，不能把常壓泡沫量直接當倉內有效體積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check meter location, pressure convention and gas-liquid proportion and assess pressurized stability through qualified testing; attach reference conditions to volume ratios rather than equating atmospheric foam volume with effective chamber volume.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設等溫理想氣體由絕對壓100增至300 kPa，初始氣體3 m³縮至1 m³；液相體積未計。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume isothermal ideal gas compressed from absolute 100 to 300 kPa; 3 m³ becomes 1 m³, excluding liquid volume.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「泡沫體積與壓縮」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Foam volume and compression\", which statement holds?","options":["刀盤功率降低就能證明改良成功，不必看進尺和地質。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","試驗流量測不到就證明改良土真正完全不透水。"],"optionsEn":["Lower cutterhead power proves successful conditioning without checking advance or geology.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Undetectable test flow proves that conditioned soil has exactly zero permeability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b136-v14-11","title":"泡沫體積與壓縮：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Foam volume and compression: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「泡沫體積與壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Foam volume and compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對流量計量測位置、壓力種類及泡沫氣液比例，使用合格試驗觀察加壓後的穩定性；所有體積比附標準狀態，不能把常壓泡沫量直接當倉內有效體積。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：使用表壓代替絕對壓會造成嚴重壓縮換算錯誤，忽略破泡又會高估可用氣泡；控制系統以錯誤體積基準比較時可能誤判材料不足或過量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check meter location, pressure convention and gas-liquid proportion and assess pressurized stability through qualified testing; attach reference conditions to volume ratios rather than equating atmospheric foam volume with effective chamber volume. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Using gauge instead of absolute pressure corrupts compression calculations, while ignored collapse overstates available bubbles. A control comparison on the wrong volume basis can falsely indicate shortage or excess conditioning. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄泡沫體積與壓縮的資料來源與適用條件。核對流量計量測位置、壓力種類及泡沫氣液比例，使用合格試驗觀察加壓後的穩定性；所有體積比附標準狀態，不能把常壓泡沫量直接當倉內有效體積。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for foam volume and compression. Check meter location, pressure convention and gas-liquid proportion and assess pressurized stability through qualified testing; attach reference conditions to volume ratios rather than equating atmospheric foam volume with effective chamber volume.","failure":"注意干擾：使用表壓代替絕對壓會造成嚴重壓縮換算錯誤，忽略破泡又會高估可用氣泡；控制系統以錯誤體積基準比較時可能誤判材料不足或過量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using gauge instead of absolute pressure corrupts compression calculations, while ignored collapse overstates available bubbles. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對流量計量測位置、壓力種類及泡沫氣液比例，使用合格試驗觀察加壓後的穩定性；所有體積比附標準狀態，不能把常壓泡沫量直接當倉內有效體積。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：使用表壓代替絕對壓會造成嚴重壓縮換算錯誤，忽略破泡又會高估可用氣泡；控制系統以錯誤體積基準比較時可能誤判材料不足或過量。","textEn":"Check meter location, pressure convention and gas-liquid proportion and assess pressurized stability through qualified testing; attach reference conditions to volume ratios rather than equating atmospheric foam volume with effective chamber volume. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Using gauge instead of absolute pressure corrupts compression calculations, while ignored collapse overstates available bubbles. A control comparison on the wrong volume basis can falsely indicate shortage or excess conditioning.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄泡沫體積與壓縮的資料來源與適用條件。核對流量計量測位置、壓力種類及泡沫氣液比例，使用合格試驗觀察加壓後的穩定性；所有體積比附標準狀態，不能把常壓泡沫量直接當倉內有效體積。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for foam volume and compression. Check meter location, pressure convention and gas-liquid proportion and assess pressurized stability through qualified testing; attach reference conditions to volume ratios rather than equating atmospheric foam volume with effective chamber volume.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「泡沫體積與壓縮」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Foam volume and compression\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只保留最成功配比試驗就足以說明改良方案適用範圍。","核對流量計量測位置、壓力種類及泡沫氣液比例，使用合格試驗觀察加壓後的穩定性；所有體積比附標準狀態，不能把常壓泡沫量直接當倉內有效體積。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Retaining only the most successful trial fully describes the conditioning scheme's applicability.","Check meter location, pressure convention and gas-liquid proportion and assess pressurized stability through qualified testing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對流量計量測位置、壓力種類及泡沫氣液比例，使用合格試驗觀察加壓後的穩定性；所有體積比附標準狀態，不能把常壓泡沫量直接當倉內有效體積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check meter location, pressure convention and gas-liquid proportion and assess pressurized stability through qualified testing; attach reference conditions to volume ratios rather than equating atmospheric foam volume with effective chamber volume. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b136-v14-12","title":"泡沫體積與壓縮：失效診斷","titleEn":"Foam volume and compression: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「泡沫體積與壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Foam volume and compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用表壓代替絕對壓會造成嚴重壓縮換算錯誤，忽略破泡又會高估可用氣泡；控制系統以錯誤體積基準比較時可能誤判材料不足或過量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using gauge instead of absolute pressure corrupts compression calculations, while ignored collapse overstates available bubbles. A control comparison on the wrong volume basis can falsely indicate shortage or excess conditioning. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用表壓代替絕對壓會造成嚴重壓縮換算錯誤，忽略破泡又會高估可用氣泡；控制系統以錯誤體積基準比較時可能誤判材料不足或過量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A control comparison on the wrong volume basis can falsely indicate shortage or excess conditioning.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「常壓泡沫體積就是進入加壓土倉後的有效氣體體積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Atmospheric foam volume equals its effective gas volume inside the pressurized chamber.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用表壓代替絕對壓會造成嚴重壓縮換算錯誤，忽略破泡又會高估可用氣泡；控制系統以錯誤體積基準比較時可能誤判材料不足或過量。","textEn":"Using gauge instead of absolute pressure corrupts compression calculations, while ignored collapse overstates available bubbles. A control comparison on the wrong volume basis can falsely indicate shortage or excess conditioning.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「泡沫體積與壓縮」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Foam volume and compression\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["使用表壓代替絕對壓會造成嚴重壓縮換算錯誤，忽略破泡又會高估可用氣泡；控制系統以錯誤體積基準比較時可能誤判材料不足或過量。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","細料百分比相同的土一定具有相同塑性和改良需求。"],"optionsEn":["Using gauge instead of absolute pressure corrupts compression calculations, while ignored collapse overstates available bubbles.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Soils with equal fines content necessarily have equal plasticity and conditioning needs."],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用表壓代替絕對壓會造成嚴重壓縮換算錯誤，忽略破泡又會高估可用氣泡；控制系統以錯誤體積基準比較時可能誤判材料不足或過量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using gauge instead of absolute pressure corrupts compression calculations, while ignored collapse overstates available bubbles. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b136-v14-13","title":"粒徑與細料作用：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Grading and fines behavior: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「粒徑與細料作用」如何影響土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grading and fines behavior” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"細料影響漿體連續性與滲透，大顆粒則影響攪拌和通過能力，但相同細料百分比的礦物活性可以不同。級配分析應連到塑性與磨蝕性，不能以一條粒徑曲線決定全部改良需求。 假設乾樣2 kg中通過指定篩0.6 kg，細料比例30%；篩孔尺寸必須一併註明。 只取細膩易裝袋土會漏掉粗礫與硬塊，試驗流變因此過度理想；碰到混合面時堵塞或磨耗突然增加，原先配比試驗便無法解釋。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「粒徑與細料作用」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Fines affect matrix continuity and permeability while coarse particles affect mixing and passage. Equal fines percentages can have different mineral activity, so grading must be linked to plasticity and abrasivity rather than determining conditioning alone. For an assumed 2 kg dry sample with 0.6 kg passing a specified sieve, fines content is 30%; the sieve aperture must accompany the value. Sampling only easily bagged fine soil misses gravel and blocks, producing unrealistically favorable workability. Sudden blockage or wear in mixed ground then lies outside the original trial's representation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grading and fines behavior” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「細料百分比相同的土一定具有相同塑性和改良需求。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Soils with equal fines content necessarily have equal plasticity and conditioning needs.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「粒徑與細料作用」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grading and fines behavior”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-13-k1","title":"粒徑與細料作用","titleEn":"Grading and fines behavior","text":"細料影響漿體連續性與滲透，大顆粒則影響攪拌和通過能力，但相同細料百分比的礦物活性可以不同。級配分析應連到塑性與磨蝕性，不能以一條粒徑曲線決定全部改良需求。","textEn":"Fines affect matrix continuity and permeability while coarse particles affect mixing and passage. Equal fines percentages can have different mineral activity, so grading must be linked to plasticity and abrasivity rather than determining conditioning alone.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：細料百分比相同的土一定具有相同塑性和改良需求。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Soils with equal fines content necessarily have equal plasticity and conditioning needs. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「粒徑與細料作用」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Grading and fines behavior\" is correct?","options":["細料百分比相同的土一定具有相同塑性和改良需求。","細料影響漿體連續性與滲透，大顆粒則影響攪拌和通過能力，但相同細料百分比的礦物活性可以不同。","單一剪切速率的黏度足以代表停放和重啟流變行為。"],"optionsEn":["Soils with equal fines content necessarily have equal plasticity and conditioning needs.","Fines affect matrix continuity and permeability while coarse particles affect mixing and passage.","Viscosity at one shear rate fully represents rest and restart rheology."],"answer":1,"explanation":"細料影響漿體連續性與滲透，大顆粒則影響攪拌和通過能力，但相同細料百分比的礦物活性可以不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Fines affect matrix continuity and permeability while coarse particles affect mixing and passage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b136-v14-14","title":"粒徑與細料作用：定量估算","titleEn":"Grading and fines behavior: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「粒徑與細料作用」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grading and fines behavior” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設乾樣2 kg中通過指定篩0.6 kg，細料比例30%；篩孔尺寸必須一併註明。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For an assumed 2 kg dry sample with 0.6 kg passing a specified sieve, fines content is 30%; the sieve aperture must accompany the value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保存篩分、沉降與塑性試驗方法，對不同地層分別取樣並檢查粗粒是否在取樣時被排除；代表性評估需覆蓋過渡帶，試驗主管確認樣本能反映實際進倉土。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Document grading and plasticity methods, sampling layers separately and checking whether coarse particles were excluded during collection; include transition zones and obtain laboratory review of representativeness for chamber material.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設乾樣2 kg中通過指定篩0.6 kg，細料比例30%；篩孔尺寸必須一併註明。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For an assumed 2 kg dry sample with 0.6 kg passing a specified sieve, fines content is 30%; the sieve aperture must accompany the value.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「粒徑與細料作用」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Grading and fines behavior\", which statement holds?","options":["添加總量達標就證明各區材料分布一定均勻。","材料短時試驗合格就保證任何溫度和停放時間都相容。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Meeting the total addition quantity proves uniform distribution throughout the chamber.","Passing a short trial guarantees compatibility at every temperature and storage duration.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b136-v14-15","title":"粒徑與細料作用：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Grading and fines behavior: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「粒徑與細料作用」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grading and fines behavior” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保存篩分、沉降與塑性試驗方法，對不同地層分別取樣並檢查粗粒是否在取樣時被排除；代表性評估需覆蓋過渡帶，試驗主管確認樣本能反映實際進倉土。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只取細膩易裝袋土會漏掉粗礫與硬塊，試驗流變因此過度理想；碰到混合面時堵塞或磨耗突然增加，原先配比試驗便無法解釋。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Document grading and plasticity methods, sampling layers separately and checking whether coarse particles were excluded during collection; include transition zones and obtain laboratory review of representativeness for chamber material. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Sampling only easily bagged fine soil misses gravel and blocks, producing unrealistically favorable workability. Sudden blockage or wear in mixed ground then lies outside the original trial's representation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄粒徑與細料作用的資料來源與適用條件。保存篩分、沉降與塑性試驗方法，對不同地層分別取樣並檢查粗粒是否在取樣時被排除；代表性評估需覆蓋過渡帶，試驗主管確認樣本能反映實際進倉土。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for grading and fines behavior. Document grading and plasticity methods, sampling layers separately and checking whether coarse particles were excluded during collection; include transition zones and obtain laboratory review of representativeness for chamber material.","failure":"注意干擾：只取細膩易裝袋土會漏掉粗礫與硬塊，試驗流變因此過度理想；碰到混合面時堵塞或磨耗突然增加，原先配比試驗便無法解釋。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sampling only easily bagged fine soil misses gravel and blocks, producing unrealistically favorable workability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保存篩分、沉降與塑性試驗方法，對不同地層分別取樣並檢查粗粒是否在取樣時被排除；代表性評估需覆蓋過渡帶，試驗主管確認樣本能反映實際進倉土。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只取細膩易裝袋土會漏掉粗礫與硬塊，試驗流變因此過度理想；碰到混合面時堵塞或磨耗突然增加，原先配比試驗便無法解釋。","textEn":"Document grading and plasticity methods, sampling layers separately and checking whether coarse particles were excluded during collection; include transition zones and obtain laboratory review of representativeness for chamber material. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Sampling only easily bagged fine soil misses gravel and blocks, producing unrealistically favorable workability. Sudden blockage or wear in mixed ground then lies outside the original trial's representation.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄粒徑與細料作用的資料來源與適用條件。保存篩分、沉降與塑性試驗方法，對不同地層分別取樣並檢查粗粒是否在取樣時被排除；代表性評估需覆蓋過渡帶，試驗主管確認樣本能反映實際進倉土。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for grading and fines behavior. Document grading and plasticity methods, sampling layers separately and checking whether coarse particles were excluded during collection; include transition zones and obtain laboratory review of representativeness for chamber material.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「粒徑與細料作用」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Grading and fines behavior\"?","options":["保存篩分、沉降與塑性試驗方法，對不同地層分別取樣並檢查粗粒是否在取樣時被排除；代表性評估需覆蓋過渡帶，試驗主管確認樣本能反映實際進倉土。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","改良土越稀越容易流動，就一定越有利於穩定支護。"],"optionsEn":["Document grading and plasticity methods, sampling layers separately and checking whether coarse particles were excluded during collection.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","More fluid conditioned soil is necessarily better for stable face support."],"answer":0,"explanation":"保存篩分、沉降與塑性試驗方法，對不同地層分別取樣並檢查粗粒是否在取樣時被排除；代表性評估需覆蓋過渡帶，試驗主管確認樣本能反映實際進倉土。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Document grading and plasticity methods, sampling layers separately and checking whether coarse particles were excluded during collection; include transition zones and obtain laboratory review of representativeness for chamber material. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b136-v14-16","title":"粒徑與細料作用：失效診斷","titleEn":"Grading and fines behavior: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「粒徑與細料作用」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grading and fines behavior” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只取細膩易裝袋土會漏掉粗礫與硬塊，試驗流變因此過度理想；碰到混合面時堵塞或磨耗突然增加，原先配比試驗便無法解釋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sampling only easily bagged fine soil misses gravel and blocks, producing unrealistically favorable workability. Sudden blockage or wear in mixed ground then lies outside the original trial's representation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只取細膩易裝袋土會漏掉粗礫與硬塊，試驗流變因此過度理想；碰到混合面時堵塞或磨耗突然增加，原先配比試驗便無法解釋。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Sudden blockage or wear in mixed ground then lies outside the original trial's representation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「細料百分比相同的土一定具有相同塑性和改良需求。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Soils with equal fines content necessarily have equal plasticity and conditioning needs.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只取細膩易裝袋土會漏掉粗礫與硬塊，試驗流變因此過度理想；碰到混合面時堵塞或磨耗突然增加，原先配比試驗便無法解釋。","textEn":"Sampling only easily bagged fine soil misses gravel and blocks, producing unrealistically favorable workability. Sudden blockage or wear in mixed ground then lies outside the original trial's representation.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粒徑與細料作用」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Grading and fines behavior\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只取細膩易裝袋土會漏掉粗礫與硬塊，試驗流變因此過度理想；碰到混合面時堵塞或磨耗突然增加，原先配比試驗便無法解釋。","單一剪切速率的黏度足以代表停放和重啟流變行為。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Sampling only easily bagged fine soil misses gravel and blocks, producing unrealistically favorable workability.","Viscosity at one shear rate fully represents rest and restart rheology."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只取細膩易裝袋土會漏掉粗礫與硬塊，試驗流變因此過度理想；碰到混合面時堵塞或磨耗突然增加，原先配比試驗便無法解釋。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sampling only easily bagged fine soil misses gravel and blocks, producing unrealistically favorable workability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b136-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「流變屈服與黏度」與「扭矩功率與能耗」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Yield stress and viscosity\" and \"Torque power and energy\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b136-v14-17","title":"流變屈服與黏度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Yield stress and viscosity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「流變屈服與黏度」如何影響土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Yield stress and viscosity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"改良土可能需超過屈服應力才開始流動，之後流動阻力仍隨剪切速率改變。單點黏度不能代表整條流動曲線，且停放後觸變恢復使重新啟動條件不同於持續攪拌。 假設Bingham示意τy=2 kPa、μp=0.5 kPa·s、剪率4 s⁻¹，τ=τy+μpγ̇=4 kPa。 把停放後的高屈服應力當成永久變稠會導致錯誤添加，反之持續攪拌試驗又可能低估重啟阻力；缺乏歷程的數字沒有可比較意義。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「流變屈服與黏度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Conditioned ground may require a yield stress before flowing and then resist flow differently with shear rate. One viscosity value cannot represent the curve, and thixotropic recovery during rest makes restart differ from continued mixing. For assumed Bingham values τy=2 kPa, μp=0.5 kPa·s and shear rate 4 s⁻¹, τ=τy+μpγ̇=4 kPa. Treating post-rest yield increase as permanent thickening can prompt incorrect additions, while continuously mixed tests understate restart resistance. Values without shear history are not meaningfully comparable. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Yield stress and viscosity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「單一剪切速率的黏度足以代表停放和重啟流變行為。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Viscosity at one shear rate fully represents rest and restart rheology.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「流變屈服與黏度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Yield stress and viscosity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-17-k1","title":"流變屈服與黏度","titleEn":"Yield stress and viscosity","text":"改良土可能需超過屈服應力才開始流動，之後流動阻力仍隨剪切速率改變。單點黏度不能代表整條流動曲線，且停放後觸變恢復使重新啟動條件不同於持續攪拌。","textEn":"Conditioned ground may require a yield stress before flowing and then resist flow differently with shear rate. One viscosity value cannot represent the curve, and thixotropic recovery during rest makes restart differ from continued mixing.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：單一剪切速率的黏度足以代表停放和重啟流變行為。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Viscosity at one shear rate fully represents rest and restart rheology. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「流變屈服與黏度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Yield stress and viscosity\" is correct?","options":["單一剪切速率的黏度足以代表停放和重啟流變行為。","刀盤功率降低就能證明改良成功，不必看進尺和地質。","改良土可能需超過屈服應力才開始流動，之後流動阻力仍隨剪切速率改變。"],"optionsEn":["Viscosity at one shear rate fully represents rest and restart rheology.","Lower cutterhead power proves successful conditioning without checking advance or geology.","Conditioned ground may require a yield stress before flowing and then resist flow differently with shear rate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"改良土可能需超過屈服應力才開始流動，之後流動阻力仍隨剪切速率改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Conditioned ground may require a yield stress before flowing and then resist flow differently with shear rate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b136-v14-18","title":"流變屈服與黏度：定量估算","titleEn":"Yield stress and viscosity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「流變屈服與黏度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Yield stress and viscosity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設Bingham示意τy=2 kPa、μp=0.5 kPa·s、剪率4 s⁻¹，τ=τy+μpγ̇=4 kPa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed Bingham values τy=2 kPa, μp=0.5 kPa·s and shear rate 4 s⁻¹, τ=τy+μpγ̇=4 kPa. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在適合粗粒尺度的試驗裝置量測多剪率及停放再啟動曲線，記錄溫度和歷程；比較模型殘差與重複性，只有校準範圍內才可用該式描述，不能直接換算機器扭矩指令。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure multiple shear rates and rest-restart curves in equipment appropriate to particle size, recording temperature and history; use the model only within calibrated behavior and never convert it directly into a machine torque instruction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設Bingham示意τy=2 kPa、μp=0.5 kPa·s、剪率4 s⁻¹，τ=τy+μpγ̇=4 kPa。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed Bingham values τy=2 kPa, μp=0.5 kPa·s and shear rate 4 s⁻¹, τ=τy+μpγ̇=4 kPa.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「流變屈服與黏度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Yield stress and viscosity\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","試驗流量測不到就證明改良土真正完全不透水。","只保留最成功配比試驗就足以說明改良方案適用範圍。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Undetectable test flow proves that conditioned soil has exactly zero permeability.","Retaining only the most successful trial fully describes the conditioning scheme's applicability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b136-v14-19","title":"流變屈服與黏度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Yield stress and viscosity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「流變屈服與黏度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Yield stress and viscosity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在適合粗粒尺度的試驗裝置量測多剪率及停放再啟動曲線，記錄溫度和歷程；比較模型殘差與重複性，只有校準範圍內才可用該式描述，不能直接換算機器扭矩指令。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把停放後的高屈服應力當成永久變稠會導致錯誤添加，反之持續攪拌試驗又可能低估重啟阻力；缺乏歷程的數字沒有可比較意義。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure multiple shear rates and rest-restart curves in equipment appropriate to particle size, recording temperature and history; use the model only within calibrated behavior and never convert it directly into a machine torque instruction. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Treating post-rest yield increase as permanent thickening can prompt incorrect additions, while continuously mixed tests understate restart resistance. Values without shear history are not meaningfully comparable. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄流變屈服與黏度的資料來源與適用條件。在適合粗粒尺度的試驗裝置量測多剪率及停放再啟動曲線，記錄溫度和歷程；比較模型殘差與重複性，只有校準範圍內才可用該式描述，不能直接換算機器扭矩指令。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for yield stress and viscosity. Measure multiple shear rates and rest-restart curves in equipment appropriate to particle size, recording temperature and history; use the model only within calibrated behavior and never convert it directly into a machine torque instruction.","failure":"注意干擾：把停放後的高屈服應力當成永久變稠會導致錯誤添加，反之持續攪拌試驗又可能低估重啟阻力；缺乏歷程的數字沒有可比較意義。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating post-rest yield increase as permanent thickening can prompt incorrect additions, while continuously mixed tests understate restart resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在適合粗粒尺度的試驗裝置量測多剪率及停放再啟動曲線，記錄溫度和歷程；比較模型殘差與重複性，只有校準範圍內才可用該式描述，不能直接換算機器扭矩指令。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把停放後的高屈服應力當成永久變稠會導致錯誤添加，反之持續攪拌試驗又可能低估重啟阻力；缺乏歷程的數字沒有可比較意義。","textEn":"Measure multiple shear rates and rest-restart curves in equipment appropriate to particle size, recording temperature and history; use the model only within calibrated behavior and never convert it directly into a machine torque instruction. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Treating post-rest yield increase as permanent thickening can prompt incorrect additions, while continuously mixed tests understate restart resistance. Values without shear history are not meaningfully comparable.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄流變屈服與黏度的資料來源與適用條件。在適合粗粒尺度的試驗裝置量測多剪率及停放再啟動曲線，記錄溫度和歷程；比較模型殘差與重複性，只有校準範圍內才可用該式描述，不能直接換算機器扭矩指令。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for yield stress and viscosity. Measure multiple shear rates and rest-restart curves in equipment appropriate to particle size, recording temperature and history; use the model only within calibrated behavior and never convert it directly into a machine torque instruction.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「流變屈服與黏度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Yield stress and viscosity\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在適合粗粒尺度的試驗裝置量測多剪率及停放再啟動曲線，記錄溫度和歷程；比較模型殘差與重複性，只有校準範圍內才可用該式描述，不能直接換算機器扭矩指令。","乾基含水率與水占濕土重量比例永遠可以互換。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure multiple shear rates and rest-restart curves in equipment appropriate to particle size, recording temperature and history.","Dry-basis moisture content and water fraction of wet mass are always interchangeable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在適合粗粒尺度的試驗裝置量測多剪率及停放再啟動曲線，記錄溫度和歷程；比較模型殘差與重複性，只有校準範圍內才可用該式描述，不能直接換算機器扭矩指令。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure multiple shear rates and rest-restart curves in equipment appropriate to particle size, recording temperature and history; use the model only within calibrated behavior and never convert it directly into a machine torque instruction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b136-v14-20","title":"流變屈服與黏度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Yield stress and viscosity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「流變屈服與黏度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Yield stress and viscosity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把停放後的高屈服應力當成永久變稠會導致錯誤添加，反之持續攪拌試驗又可能低估重啟阻力；缺乏歷程的數字沒有可比較意義。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating post-rest yield increase as permanent thickening can prompt incorrect additions, while continuously mixed tests understate restart resistance. Values without shear history are not meaningfully comparable. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把停放後的高屈服應力當成永久變稠會導致錯誤添加，反之持續攪拌試驗又可能低估重啟阻力；缺乏歷程的數字沒有可比較意義。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Values without shear history are not meaningfully comparable.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「單一剪切速率的黏度足以代表停放和重啟流變行為。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Viscosity at one shear rate fully represents rest and restart rheology.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把停放後的高屈服應力當成永久變稠會導致錯誤添加，反之持續攪拌試驗又可能低估重啟阻力；缺乏歷程的數字沒有可比較意義。","textEn":"Treating post-rest yield increase as permanent thickening can prompt incorrect additions, while continuously mixed tests understate restart resistance. Values without shear history are not meaningfully comparable.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「流變屈服與黏度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Yield stress and viscosity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","刀盤功率降低就能證明改良成功，不必看進尺和地質。","把停放後的高屈服應力當成永久變稠會導致錯誤添加，反之持續攪拌試驗又可能低估重啟阻力；缺乏歷程的數字沒有可比較意義。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Lower cutterhead power proves successful conditioning without checking advance or geology.","Treating post-rest yield increase as permanent thickening can prompt incorrect additions, while continuously mixed tests understate restart resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把停放後的高屈服應力當成永久變稠會導致錯誤添加，反之持續攪拌試驗又可能低估重啟阻力；缺乏歷程的數字沒有可比較意義。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating post-rest yield increase as permanent thickening can prompt incorrect additions, while continuously mixed tests understate restart resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b136-v14-21","title":"扭矩功率與能耗：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Torque power and energy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「扭矩功率與能耗」如何影響土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Torque power and energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"刀盤功率等於扭矩乘角速度，能源變化可提示磨耗、黏附或材料改良差異，但也受地層強度和推進量影響。將能耗按開挖體積規一化才能做較公平的比較，仍不能單獨確定成因。 假設扭矩1 MN·m、轉速2 rpm，P=T×2πn/60=209.4 kW；非額定能力或推薦轉速。 低功率可能來自低進尺而非改良成功，高功率也可能是新硬層而非泡沫不足；若無地質和產量校正，控制調整會追逐錯誤訊號。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「扭矩功率與能耗」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cutterhead power is torque times angular speed. Changes may indicate wear, adhesion or conditioning, but also strength and penetration. Volume-normalized energy improves comparison without uniquely identifying the cause. For assumed torque 1 MN·m and speed 2 rpm, P=T×2πn/60=209.4 kW; these are neither ratings nor recommended settings. Low power may reflect reduced excavation rather than successful conditioning, and high power may reflect harder ground rather than insufficient foam. Without geology and production correction, adjustments chase the wrong signal. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Torque power and energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀盤功率降低就能證明改良成功，不必看進尺和地質。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower cutterhead power proves successful conditioning without checking advance or geology.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「扭矩功率與能耗」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Torque power and energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-21-k1","title":"扭矩功率與能耗","titleEn":"Torque power and energy","text":"刀盤功率等於扭矩乘角速度，能源變化可提示磨耗、黏附或材料改良差異，但也受地層強度和推進量影響。將能耗按開挖體積規一化才能做較公平的比較，仍不能單獨確定成因。","textEn":"Cutterhead power is torque times angular speed. Changes may indicate wear, adhesion or conditioning, but also strength and penetration.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀盤功率降低就能證明改良成功，不必看進尺和地質。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower cutterhead power proves successful conditioning without checking advance or geology. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「扭矩功率與能耗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Torque power and energy\" is correct?","options":["刀盤功率等於扭矩乘角速度，能源變化可提示磨耗、黏附或材料改良差異，但也受地層強度和推進量影響。","刀盤功率降低就能證明改良成功，不必看進尺和地質。","添加總量達標就證明各區材料分布一定均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Cutterhead power is torque times angular speed.","Lower cutterhead power proves successful conditioning without checking advance or geology.","Meeting the total addition quantity proves uniform distribution throughout the chamber."],"answer":0,"explanation":"刀盤功率等於扭矩乘角速度，能源變化可提示磨耗、黏附或材料改良差異，但也受地層強度和推進量影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cutterhead power is torque times angular speed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b136-v14-22","title":"扭矩功率與能耗：定量估算","titleEn":"Torque power and energy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「扭矩功率與能耗」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Torque power and energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設扭矩1 MN·m、轉速2 rpm，P=T×2πn/60=209.4 kW；非額定能力或推薦轉速。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed torque 1 MN·m and speed 2 rpm, P=T×2πn/60=209.4 kW; these are neither ratings nor recommended settings. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步扭矩、轉速、推進、地質與改良材料紀錄，剔除空轉及維修段後比較單位體積能量；任何效率結論需同時檢查壓力穩定與沉陷，不能用低功率作唯一最佳化目標。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize torque, speed, advance, geology and conditioning records, excluding idle and maintenance periods before comparing energy per volume; efficiency conclusions must also check pressure and settlement rather than minimizing power alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設扭矩1 MN·m、轉速2 rpm，P=T×2πn/60=209.4 kW；非額定能力或推薦轉速。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed torque 1 MN·m and speed 2 rpm, P=T×2πn/60=209.4 kW; these are neither ratings nor recommended settings.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「扭矩功率與能耗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Torque power and energy\", which statement holds?","options":["材料短時試驗合格就保證任何溫度和停放時間都相容。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","改良土越稀越容易流動，就一定越有利於穩定支護。"],"optionsEn":["Passing a short trial guarantees compatibility at every temperature and storage duration.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","More fluid conditioned soil is necessarily better for stable face support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b136-v14-23","title":"扭矩功率與能耗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Torque power and energy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「扭矩功率與能耗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Torque power and energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步扭矩、轉速、推進、地質與改良材料紀錄，剔除空轉及維修段後比較單位體積能量；任何效率結論需同時檢查壓力穩定與沉陷，不能用低功率作唯一最佳化目標。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：低功率可能來自低進尺而非改良成功，高功率也可能是新硬層而非泡沫不足；若無地質和產量校正，控制調整會追逐錯誤訊號。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize torque, speed, advance, geology and conditioning records, excluding idle and maintenance periods before comparing energy per volume; efficiency conclusions must also check pressure and settlement rather than minimizing power alone. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Low power may reflect reduced excavation rather than successful conditioning, and high power may reflect harder ground rather than insufficient foam. Without geology and production correction, adjustments chase the wrong signal. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄扭矩功率與能耗的資料來源與適用條件。同步扭矩、轉速、推進、地質與改良材料紀錄，剔除空轉及維修段後比較單位體積能量；任何效率結論需同時檢查壓力穩定與沉陷，不能用低功率作唯一最佳化目標。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for torque power and energy. Synchronize torque, speed, advance, geology and conditioning records, excluding idle and maintenance periods before comparing energy per volume; efficiency conclusions must also check pressure and settlement rather than minimizing power alone.","failure":"注意干擾：低功率可能來自低進尺而非改良成功，高功率也可能是新硬層而非泡沫不足；若無地質和產量校正，控制調整會追逐錯誤訊號。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Low power may reflect reduced excavation rather than successful conditioning, and high power may reflect harder ground rather than insufficient foam. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步扭矩、轉速、推進、地質與改良材料紀錄，剔除空轉及維修段後比較單位體積能量；任何效率結論需同時檢查壓力穩定與沉陷，不能用低功率作唯一最佳化目標。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：低功率可能來自低進尺而非改良成功，高功率也可能是新硬層而非泡沫不足；若無地質和產量校正，控制調整會追逐錯誤訊號。","textEn":"Synchronize torque, speed, advance, geology and conditioning records, excluding idle and maintenance periods before comparing energy per volume; efficiency conclusions must also check pressure and settlement rather than minimizing power alone. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Low power may reflect reduced excavation rather than successful conditioning, and high power may reflect harder ground rather than insufficient foam. Without geology and production correction, adjustments chase the wrong signal.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄扭矩功率與能耗的資料來源與適用條件。同步扭矩、轉速、推進、地質與改良材料紀錄，剔除空轉及維修段後比較單位體積能量；任何效率結論需同時檢查壓力穩定與沉陷，不能用低功率作唯一最佳化目標。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for torque power and energy. Synchronize torque, speed, advance, geology and conditioning records, excluding idle and maintenance periods before comparing energy per volume; efficiency conclusions must also check pressure and settlement rather than minimizing power alone.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「扭矩功率與能耗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Torque power and energy\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","常壓泡沫體積就是進入加壓土倉後的有效氣體體積。","同步扭矩、轉速、推進、地質與改良材料紀錄，剔除空轉及維修段後比較單位體積能量；任何效率結論需同時檢查壓力穩定與沉陷，不能用低功率作唯一最佳化目標。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Atmospheric foam volume equals its effective gas volume inside the pressurized chamber.","Synchronize torque, speed, advance, geology and conditioning records, excluding idle and maintenance periods before comparing energy per volume."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步扭矩、轉速、推進、地質與改良材料紀錄，剔除空轉及維修段後比較單位體積能量；任何效率結論需同時檢查壓力穩定與沉陷，不能用低功率作唯一最佳化目標。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize torque, speed, advance, geology and conditioning records, excluding idle and maintenance periods before comparing energy per volume; efficiency conclusions must also check pressure and settlement rather than minimizing power alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b136-v14-24","title":"扭矩功率與能耗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Torque power and energy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「扭矩功率與能耗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Torque power and energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"低功率可能來自低進尺而非改良成功，高功率也可能是新硬層而非泡沫不足；若無地質和產量校正，控制調整會追逐錯誤訊號。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Low power may reflect reduced excavation rather than successful conditioning, and high power may reflect harder ground rather than insufficient foam. Without geology and production correction, adjustments chase the wrong signal. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：低功率可能來自低進尺而非改良成功，高功率也可能是新硬層而非泡沫不足；若無地質和產量校正，控制調整會追逐錯誤訊號。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Without geology and production correction, adjustments chase the wrong signal.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀盤功率降低就能證明改良成功，不必看進尺和地質。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower cutterhead power proves successful conditioning without checking advance or geology.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"低功率可能來自低進尺而非改良成功，高功率也可能是新硬層而非泡沫不足；若無地質和產量校正，控制調整會追逐錯誤訊號。","textEn":"Low power may reflect reduced excavation rather than successful conditioning, and high power may reflect harder ground rather than insufficient foam. Without geology and production correction, adjustments chase the wrong signal.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「扭矩功率與能耗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Torque power and energy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["低功率可能來自低進尺而非改良成功，高功率也可能是新硬層而非泡沫不足；若無地質和產量校正，控制調整會追逐錯誤訊號。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","添加總量達標就證明各區材料分布一定均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Low power may reflect reduced excavation rather than successful conditioning, and high power may reflect harder ground rather than insufficient foam.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Meeting the total addition quantity proves uniform distribution throughout the chamber."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低功率可能來自低進尺而非改良成功，高功率也可能是新硬層而非泡沫不足；若無地質和產量校正，控制調整會追逐錯誤訊號。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Low power may reflect reduced excavation rather than successful conditioning, and high power may reflect harder ground rather than insufficient foam. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b136-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「添加收支與混合均勻」與「滲透與壓力保持」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Addition balance and mixing uniformity\" and \"Permeability and pressure retention\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b136-v14-25","title":"添加收支與混合均勻：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Addition balance and mixing uniformity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「添加收支與混合均勻」如何影響土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Addition balance and mixing uniformity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"添加物總量不代表全倉分布均勻，噴口阻塞或混合死角會造成局部乾團與稀漿並存。收支需按時間與原土體積對齊，並以多位置樣本檢查離散，不能只看泵浦累計量。 假設一段原土40 m³加入液體2 m³，體積比5%；此示意不指定任何材料配方。 總量達標但部分噴口失效仍會造成局部失控，時間對錯環則使每環比值失真；將差異全歸於土質可能掩蓋可修復的設備問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「添加收支與混合均勻」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Total additive volume does not prove uniform chamber distribution. Blocked delivery or dead zones can leave dry lumps beside dilute slurry. Align quantities with original-soil volume and time and check spatial variability, not only pump totals. An assumed 2 m³ of liquid added to 40 m³ of original ground gives a 5% ratio; this illustration specifies no material recipe. Adequate totals with failed outlets still produce local problems, and assigning delayed delivery to the wrong ring distorts ratios. Blaming all variability on soil can conceal a correctable equipment fault. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Addition balance and mixing uniformity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「添加總量達標就證明各區材料分布一定均勻。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Meeting the total addition quantity proves uniform distribution throughout the chamber.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「添加收支與混合均勻」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Addition balance and mixing uniformity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-25-k1","title":"添加收支與混合均勻","titleEn":"Addition balance and mixing uniformity","text":"添加物總量不代表全倉分布均勻，噴口阻塞或混合死角會造成局部乾團與稀漿並存。收支需按時間與原土體積對齊，並以多位置樣本檢查離散，不能只看泵浦累計量。","textEn":"Total additive volume does not prove uniform chamber distribution. Blocked delivery or dead zones can leave dry lumps beside dilute slurry.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：添加總量達標就證明各區材料分布一定均勻。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Meeting the total addition quantity proves uniform distribution throughout the chamber. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「添加收支與混合均勻」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Addition balance and mixing uniformity\" is correct?","options":["添加總量達標就證明各區材料分布一定均勻。","添加物總量不代表全倉分布均勻，噴口阻塞或混合死角會造成局部乾團與稀漿並存。","試驗流量測不到就證明改良土真正完全不透水。"],"optionsEn":["Meeting the total addition quantity proves uniform distribution throughout the chamber.","Total additive volume does not prove uniform chamber distribution.","Undetectable test flow proves that conditioned soil has exactly zero permeability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"添加物總量不代表全倉分布均勻，噴口阻塞或混合死角會造成局部乾團與稀漿並存。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Total additive volume does not prove uniform chamber distribution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b136-v14-26","title":"添加收支與混合均勻：定量估算","titleEn":"Addition balance and mixing uniformity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「添加收支與混合均勻」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Addition balance and mixing uniformity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設一段原土40 m³加入液體2 m³，體積比5%；此示意不指定任何材料配方。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed 2 m³ of liquid added to 40 m³ of original ground gives a 5% ratio; this illustration specifies no material recipe. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以儲槽變化和流量計交叉核對添加量，檢查輸送延遲與管線殘留；多點抽樣比較含水和可塑性，異常分布須先查設備路徑，再由專業團隊評估試驗配比。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Cross-check additions using tank levels and meters and account for delivery delay and retained line contents; compare moisture and workability across samples, investigating delivery paths before specialists reconsider trial proportions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設一段原土40 m³加入液體2 m³，體積比5%；此示意不指定任何材料配方。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed 2 m³ of liquid added to 40 m³ of original ground gives a 5% ratio; this illustration specifies no material recipe.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「添加收支與混合均勻」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Addition balance and mixing uniformity\", which statement holds?","options":["只保留最成功配比試驗就足以說明改良方案適用範圍。","乾基含水率與水占濕土重量比例永遠可以互換。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Retaining only the most successful trial fully describes the conditioning scheme's applicability.","Dry-basis moisture content and water fraction of wet mass are always interchangeable.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b136-v14-27","title":"添加收支與混合均勻：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Addition balance and mixing uniformity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「添加收支與混合均勻」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Addition balance and mixing uniformity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以儲槽變化和流量計交叉核對添加量，檢查輸送延遲與管線殘留；多點抽樣比較含水和可塑性，異常分布須先查設備路徑，再由專業團隊評估試驗配比。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：總量達標但部分噴口失效仍會造成局部失控，時間對錯環則使每環比值失真；將差異全歸於土質可能掩蓋可修復的設備問題。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Cross-check additions using tank levels and meters and account for delivery delay and retained line contents; compare moisture and workability across samples, investigating delivery paths before specialists reconsider trial proportions. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Adequate totals with failed outlets still produce local problems, and assigning delayed delivery to the wrong ring distorts ratios. Blaming all variability on soil can conceal a correctable equipment fault. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄添加收支與混合均勻的資料來源與適用條件。以儲槽變化和流量計交叉核對添加量，檢查輸送延遲與管線殘留；多點抽樣比較含水和可塑性，異常分布須先查設備路徑，再由專業團隊評估試驗配比。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for addition balance and mixing uniformity. Cross-check additions using tank levels and meters and account for delivery delay and retained line contents; compare moisture and workability across samples, investigating delivery paths before specialists reconsider trial proportions.","failure":"注意干擾：總量達標但部分噴口失效仍會造成局部失控，時間對錯環則使每環比值失真；將差異全歸於土質可能掩蓋可修復的設備問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adequate totals with failed outlets still produce local problems, and assigning delayed delivery to the wrong ring distorts ratios. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以儲槽變化和流量計交叉核對添加量，檢查輸送延遲與管線殘留；多點抽樣比較含水和可塑性，異常分布須先查設備路徑，再由專業團隊評估試驗配比。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：總量達標但部分噴口失效仍會造成局部失控，時間對錯環則使每環比值失真；將差異全歸於土質可能掩蓋可修復的設備問題。","textEn":"Cross-check additions using tank levels and meters and account for delivery delay and retained line contents; compare moisture and workability across samples, investigating delivery paths before specialists reconsider trial proportions. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Adequate totals with failed outlets still produce local problems, and assigning delayed delivery to the wrong ring distorts ratios. Blaming all variability on soil can conceal a correctable equipment fault.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄添加收支與混合均勻的資料來源與適用條件。以儲槽變化和流量計交叉核對添加量，檢查輸送延遲與管線殘留；多點抽樣比較含水和可塑性，異常分布須先查設備路徑，再由專業團隊評估試驗配比。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for addition balance and mixing uniformity. Cross-check additions using tank levels and meters and account for delivery delay and retained line contents; compare moisture and workability across samples, investigating delivery paths before specialists reconsider trial proportions.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「添加收支與混合均勻」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Addition balance and mixing uniformity\"?","options":["以儲槽變化和流量計交叉核對添加量，檢查輸送延遲與管線殘留；多點抽樣比較含水和可塑性，異常分布須先查設備路徑，再由專業團隊評估試驗配比。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","細料百分比相同的土一定具有相同塑性和改良需求。"],"optionsEn":["Cross-check additions using tank levels and meters and account for delivery delay and retained line contents.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Soils with equal fines content necessarily have equal plasticity and conditioning needs."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以儲槽變化和流量計交叉核對添加量，檢查輸送延遲與管線殘留；多點抽樣比較含水和可塑性，異常分布須先查設備路徑，再由專業團隊評估試驗配比。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Cross-check additions using tank levels and meters and account for delivery delay and retained line contents; compare moisture and workability across samples, investigating delivery paths before specialists reconsider trial proportions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b136-v14-28","title":"添加收支與混合均勻：失效診斷","titleEn":"Addition balance and mixing uniformity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「添加收支與混合均勻」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Addition balance and mixing uniformity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"總量達標但部分噴口失效仍會造成局部失控，時間對錯環則使每環比值失真；將差異全歸於土質可能掩蓋可修復的設備問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adequate totals with failed outlets still produce local problems, and assigning delayed delivery to the wrong ring distorts ratios. Blaming all variability on soil can conceal a correctable equipment fault. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：總量達標但部分噴口失效仍會造成局部失控，時間對錯環則使每環比值失真；將差異全歸於土質可能掩蓋可修復的設備問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Blaming all variability on soil can conceal a correctable equipment fault.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「添加總量達標就證明各區材料分布一定均勻。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Meeting the total addition quantity proves uniform distribution throughout the chamber.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"總量達標但部分噴口失效仍會造成局部失控，時間對錯環則使每環比值失真；將差異全歸於土質可能掩蓋可修復的設備問題。","textEn":"Adequate totals with failed outlets still produce local problems, and assigning delayed delivery to the wrong ring distorts ratios. Blaming all variability on soil can conceal a correctable equipment fault.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「添加收支與混合均勻」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Addition balance and mixing uniformity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","總量達標但部分噴口失效仍會造成局部失控，時間對錯環則使每環比值失真；將差異全歸於土質可能掩蓋可修復的設備問題。","試驗流量測不到就證明改良土真正完全不透水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Adequate totals with failed outlets still produce local problems, and assigning delayed delivery to the wrong ring distorts ratios.","Undetectable test flow proves that conditioned soil has exactly zero permeability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"總量達標但部分噴口失效仍會造成局部失控，時間對錯環則使每環比值失真；將差異全歸於土質可能掩蓋可修復的設備問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adequate totals with failed outlets still produce local problems, and assigning delayed delivery to the wrong ring distorts ratios. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b136-v14-29","title":"滲透與壓力保持：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Permeability and pressure retention: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「滲透與壓力保持」如何影響土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Permeability and pressure retention” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"改良土的低滲透性有助於保持壓差，但試驗有效性取決於孔隙結構、壓密和氣泡狀態。過低流量也可能是裝置堵塞，不能把所有零讀值都解讀成理想材料，應確認量測下限。 假設k=10⁻⁷ m/s、面積0.01 m²、梯度10，Q=10⁻⁸ m³/s=0.0006 L/min，需足夠量測靈敏度。 裝置堵塞可產生極佳的假低滲透，氣泡壓縮則造成初期流量遲滯；若據此認為任何停機都能保持壓力，會把實驗假象當現場保障。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滲透與壓力保持」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Limited permeability helps sustain pressure difference, but testing depends on pore structure, compaction and gas state. Near-zero flow can also mean apparatus blockage, so instrument detection limits and continuity require verification. Assume k=10⁻⁷ m/s, area 0.01 m² and gradient 10; Q=10⁻⁸ m³/s=0.0006 L/min, requiring sufficient sensitivity. Apparatus blockage creates falsely excellent low permeability, and bubble compression delays initial flow. Assuming pressure will then persist through any stoppage turns a test artifact into an unjustified field assurance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Permeability and pressure retention” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「試驗流量測不到就證明改良土真正完全不透水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Undetectable test flow proves that conditioned soil has exactly zero permeability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滲透與壓力保持」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Permeability and pressure retention”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-29-k1","title":"滲透與壓力保持","titleEn":"Permeability and pressure retention","text":"改良土的低滲透性有助於保持壓差，但試驗有效性取決於孔隙結構、壓密和氣泡狀態。過低流量也可能是裝置堵塞，不能把所有零讀值都解讀成理想材料，應確認量測下限。","textEn":"Limited permeability helps sustain pressure difference, but testing depends on pore structure, compaction and gas state. Near-zero flow can also mean apparatus blockage, so instrument detection limits and continuity require verification.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：試驗流量測不到就證明改良土真正完全不透水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Undetectable test flow proves that conditioned soil has exactly zero permeability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「滲透與壓力保持」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Permeability and pressure retention\" is correct?","options":["試驗流量測不到就證明改良土真正完全不透水。","材料短時試驗合格就保證任何溫度和停放時間都相容。","改良土的低滲透性有助於保持壓差，但試驗有效性取決於孔隙結構、壓密和氣泡狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Undetectable test flow proves that conditioned soil has exactly zero permeability.","Passing a short trial guarantees compatibility at every temperature and storage duration.","Limited permeability helps sustain pressure difference, but testing depends on pore structure, compaction and gas state."],"answer":2,"explanation":"改良土的低滲透性有助於保持壓差，但試驗有效性取決於孔隙結構、壓密和氣泡狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Limited permeability helps sustain pressure difference, but testing depends on pore structure, compaction and gas state. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b136-v14-30","title":"滲透與壓力保持：定量估算","titleEn":"Permeability and pressure retention: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滲透與壓力保持」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Permeability and pressure retention” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設k=10⁻⁷ m/s、面積0.01 m²、梯度10，Q=10⁻⁸ m³/s=0.0006 L/min，需足夠量測靈敏度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume k=10⁻⁷ m/s, area 0.01 m² and gradient 10; Q=10⁻⁸ m³/s=0.0006 L/min, requiring sufficient sensitivity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用適用低流量量測與空白裝置查核，觀察試體壓密和排氣歷程；結果附壓差、時間、密度及重複性，未達檢出限以界限報告，不把測不到寫成真正零滲透。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check low-flow sensitivity and a blank apparatus while observing compaction and gas release; report pressure, duration, density and repeatability, expressing below-detection results as bounds rather than true zero permeability.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設k=10⁻⁷ m/s、面積0.01 m²、梯度10，Q=10⁻⁸ m³/s=0.0006 L/min，需足夠量測靈敏度。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume k=10⁻⁷ m/s, area 0.01 m² and gradient 10; Q=10⁻⁸ m³/s=0.0006 L/min, requiring sufficient sensitivity.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「滲透與壓力保持」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Permeability and pressure retention\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","改良土越稀越容易流動，就一定越有利於穩定支護。","常壓泡沫體積就是進入加壓土倉後的有效氣體體積。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","More fluid conditioned soil is necessarily better for stable face support.","Atmospheric foam volume equals its effective gas volume inside the pressurized chamber."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b136-v14-31","title":"滲透與壓力保持：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Permeability and pressure retention: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滲透與壓力保持」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Permeability and pressure retention” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用適用低流量量測與空白裝置查核，觀察試體壓密和排氣歷程；結果附壓差、時間、密度及重複性，未達檢出限以界限報告，不把測不到寫成真正零滲透。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：裝置堵塞可產生極佳的假低滲透，氣泡壓縮則造成初期流量遲滯；若據此認為任何停機都能保持壓力，會把實驗假象當現場保障。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check low-flow sensitivity and a blank apparatus while observing compaction and gas release; report pressure, duration, density and repeatability, expressing below-detection results as bounds rather than true zero permeability. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Apparatus blockage creates falsely excellent low permeability, and bubble compression delays initial flow. Assuming pressure will then persist through any stoppage turns a test artifact into an unjustified field assurance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄滲透與壓力保持的資料來源與適用條件。使用適用低流量量測與空白裝置查核，觀察試體壓密和排氣歷程；結果附壓差、時間、密度及重複性，未達檢出限以界限報告，不把測不到寫成真正零滲透。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for permeability and pressure retention. Check low-flow sensitivity and a blank apparatus while observing compaction and gas release; report pressure, duration, density and repeatability, expressing below-detection results as bounds rather than true zero permeability.","failure":"注意干擾：裝置堵塞可產生極佳的假低滲透，氣泡壓縮則造成初期流量遲滯；若據此認為任何停機都能保持壓力，會把實驗假象當現場保障。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Apparatus blockage creates falsely excellent low permeability, and bubble compression delays initial flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用適用低流量量測與空白裝置查核，觀察試體壓密和排氣歷程；結果附壓差、時間、密度及重複性，未達檢出限以界限報告，不把測不到寫成真正零滲透。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：裝置堵塞可產生極佳的假低滲透，氣泡壓縮則造成初期流量遲滯；若據此認為任何停機都能保持壓力，會把實驗假象當現場保障。","textEn":"Check low-flow sensitivity and a blank apparatus while observing compaction and gas release; report pressure, duration, density and repeatability, expressing below-detection results as bounds rather than true zero permeability. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Apparatus blockage creates falsely excellent low permeability, and bubble compression delays initial flow. Assuming pressure will then persist through any stoppage turns a test artifact into an unjustified field assurance.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄滲透與壓力保持的資料來源與適用條件。使用適用低流量量測與空白裝置查核，觀察試體壓密和排氣歷程；結果附壓差、時間、密度及重複性，未達檢出限以界限報告，不把測不到寫成真正零滲透。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for permeability and pressure retention. Check low-flow sensitivity and a blank apparatus while observing compaction and gas release; report pressure, duration, density and repeatability, expressing below-detection results as bounds rather than true zero permeability.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「滲透與壓力保持」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Permeability and pressure retention\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","使用適用低流量量測與空白裝置查核，觀察試體壓密和排氣歷程；結果附壓差、時間、密度及重複性，未達檢出限以界限報告，不把測不到寫成真正零滲透。","單一剪切速率的黏度足以代表停放和重啟流變行為。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Check low-flow sensitivity and a blank apparatus while observing compaction and gas release.","Viscosity at one shear rate fully represents rest and restart rheology."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使用適用低流量量測與空白裝置查核，觀察試體壓密和排氣歷程；結果附壓差、時間、密度及重複性，未達檢出限以界限報告，不把測不到寫成真正零滲透。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check low-flow sensitivity and a blank apparatus while observing compaction and gas release; report pressure, duration, density and repeatability, expressing below-detection results as bounds rather than true zero permeability. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b136-v14-32","title":"滲透與壓力保持：失效診斷","titleEn":"Permeability and pressure retention: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滲透與壓力保持」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Permeability and pressure retention” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"裝置堵塞可產生極佳的假低滲透，氣泡壓縮則造成初期流量遲滯；若據此認為任何停機都能保持壓力，會把實驗假象當現場保障。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Apparatus blockage creates falsely excellent low permeability, and bubble compression delays initial flow. Assuming pressure will then persist through any stoppage turns a test artifact into an unjustified field assurance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：裝置堵塞可產生極佳的假低滲透，氣泡壓縮則造成初期流量遲滯；若據此認為任何停機都能保持壓力，會把實驗假象當現場保障。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assuming pressure will then persist through any stoppage turns a test artifact into an unjustified field assurance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「試驗流量測不到就證明改良土真正完全不透水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Undetectable test flow proves that conditioned soil has exactly zero permeability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"裝置堵塞可產生極佳的假低滲透，氣泡壓縮則造成初期流量遲滯；若據此認為任何停機都能保持壓力，會把實驗假象當現場保障。","textEn":"Apparatus blockage creates falsely excellent low permeability, and bubble compression delays initial flow. Assuming pressure will then persist through any stoppage turns a test artifact into an unjustified field assurance.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「滲透與壓力保持」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Permeability and pressure retention\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","材料短時試驗合格就保證任何溫度和停放時間都相容。","裝置堵塞可產生極佳的假低滲透，氣泡壓縮則造成初期流量遲滯；若據此認為任何停機都能保持壓力，會把實驗假象當現場保障。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Passing a short trial guarantees compatibility at every temperature and storage duration.","Apparatus blockage creates falsely excellent low permeability, and bubble compression delays initial flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"裝置堵塞可產生極佳的假低滲透，氣泡壓縮則造成初期流量遲滯；若據此認為任何停機都能保持壓力，會把實驗假象當現場保障。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Apparatus blockage creates falsely excellent low permeability, and bubble compression delays initial flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b136-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「老化與環境相容」與「改良試驗到現場移交」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Aging and environmental compatibility\" and \"Conditioning trials and field handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b136-v14-33","title":"老化與環境相容：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Aging and environmental compatibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「老化與環境相容」如何影響土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Aging and environmental compatibility” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"改良材料在土中會受時間、溫度、水質與吸附影響，短時工作性未必維持到運輸或處理。工程性能與廢土處理相互關聯，應使用經核准的相容性和環境資料，而非只追求瞬間低扭矩。 假設同法試驗初始流動指標100、2 h後80，保留比例80%；這是任意指標示例而非材料規格。 材料短期有效卻在停放後分離會使重啟困難，處理場又可能面臨不相容廢土；只記產品名稱而不記批次和水質，無法追查性能改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「老化與環境相容」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Time, temperature, water chemistry and adsorption change conditioned material, so immediate workability may not persist through handling or treatment. Engineering behavior and spoil management are linked and require approved compatibility and environmental evidence. An assumed identical-method flow index falling from 100 to 80 after 2 h has 80% retention; this arbitrary index is not a material specification. Material that separates during rest complicates restart and can create incompatible spoil for treatment. Product names without batch and water-chemistry records cannot trace the reason for changed performance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Aging and environmental compatibility” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「材料短時試驗合格就保證任何溫度和停放時間都相容。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing a short trial guarantees compatibility at every temperature and storage duration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「老化與環境相容」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Aging and environmental compatibility”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-33-k1","title":"老化與環境相容","titleEn":"Aging and environmental compatibility","text":"改良材料在土中會受時間、溫度、水質與吸附影響，短時工作性未必維持到運輸或處理。工程性能與廢土處理相互關聯，應使用經核准的相容性和環境資料，而非只追求瞬間低扭矩。","textEn":"Time, temperature, water chemistry and adsorption change conditioned material, so immediate workability may not persist through handling or treatment. Engineering behavior and spoil management are linked and require approved compatibility and environmental evidence.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：材料短時試驗合格就保證任何溫度和停放時間都相容。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing a short trial guarantees compatibility at every temperature and storage duration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「老化與環境相容」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Aging and environmental compatibility\" is correct?","options":["改良材料在土中會受時間、溫度、水質與吸附影響，短時工作性未必維持到運輸或處理。","材料短時試驗合格就保證任何溫度和停放時間都相容。","只保留最成功配比試驗就足以說明改良方案適用範圍。"],"optionsEn":["Time, temperature, water chemistry and adsorption change conditioned material, so immediate workability may not persist through handling or treatment.","Passing a short trial guarantees compatibility at every temperature and storage duration.","Retaining only the most successful trial fully describes the conditioning scheme's applicability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"改良材料在土中會受時間、溫度、水質與吸附影響，短時工作性未必維持到運輸或處理。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Time, temperature, water chemistry and adsorption change conditioned material, so immediate workability may not persist through handling or treatment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b136-v14-34","title":"老化與環境相容：定量估算","titleEn":"Aging and environmental compatibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「老化與環境相容」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Aging and environmental compatibility” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設同法試驗初始流動指標100、2 h後80，保留比例80%；這是任意指標示例而非材料規格。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed identical-method flow index falling from 100 to 80 after 2 h has 80% retention; this arbitrary index is not a material specification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在代表性水質與溫度下做時間序列試驗，保留材料批號及合規文件，將土倉與廢土處理需求一起審查；任何產品使用由專業團隊依現場核准方案決定，本課不提供化學配方。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run time-series tests at representative temperature and water chemistry with batch and compliance records, reviewing chamber and spoil-treatment needs together; specialists select products under an approved site plan, without a chemical recipe from this course.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設同法試驗初始流動指標100、2 h後80，保留比例80%；這是任意指標示例而非材料規格。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed identical-method flow index falling from 100 to 80 after 2 h has 80% retention; this arbitrary index is not a material specification.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「老化與環境相容」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Aging and environmental compatibility\", which statement holds?","options":["乾基含水率與水占濕土重量比例永遠可以互換。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","細料百分比相同的土一定具有相同塑性和改良需求。"],"optionsEn":["Dry-basis moisture content and water fraction of wet mass are always interchangeable.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Soils with equal fines content necessarily have equal plasticity and conditioning needs."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b136-v14-35","title":"老化與環境相容：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Aging and environmental compatibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「老化與環境相容」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Aging and environmental compatibility” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在代表性水質與溫度下做時間序列試驗，保留材料批號及合規文件，將土倉與廢土處理需求一起審查；任何產品使用由專業團隊依現場核准方案決定，本課不提供化學配方。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：材料短期有效卻在停放後分離會使重啟困難，處理場又可能面臨不相容廢土；只記產品名稱而不記批次和水質，無法追查性能改變。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run time-series tests at representative temperature and water chemistry with batch and compliance records, reviewing chamber and spoil-treatment needs together; specialists select products under an approved site plan, without a chemical recipe from this course. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Material that separates during rest complicates restart and can create incompatible spoil for treatment. Product names without batch and water-chemistry records cannot trace the reason for changed performance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄老化與環境相容的資料來源與適用條件。在代表性水質與溫度下做時間序列試驗，保留材料批號及合規文件，將土倉與廢土處理需求一起審查；任何產品使用由專業團隊依現場核准方案決定，本課不提供化學配方。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for aging and environmental compatibility. Run time-series tests at representative temperature and water chemistry with batch and compliance records, reviewing chamber and spoil-treatment needs together; specialists select products under an approved site plan, without a chemical recipe from this course.","failure":"注意干擾：材料短期有效卻在停放後分離會使重啟困難，處理場又可能面臨不相容廢土；只記產品名稱而不記批次和水質，無法追查性能改變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Material that separates during rest complicates restart and can create incompatible spoil for treatment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在代表性水質與溫度下做時間序列試驗，保留材料批號及合規文件，將土倉與廢土處理需求一起審查；任何產品使用由專業團隊依現場核准方案決定，本課不提供化學配方。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：材料短期有效卻在停放後分離會使重啟困難，處理場又可能面臨不相容廢土；只記產品名稱而不記批次和水質，無法追查性能改變。","textEn":"Run time-series tests at representative temperature and water chemistry with batch and compliance records, reviewing chamber and spoil-treatment needs together; specialists select products under an approved site plan, without a chemical recipe from this course. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Material that separates during rest complicates restart and can create incompatible spoil for treatment. Product names without batch and water-chemistry records cannot trace the reason for changed performance.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄老化與環境相容的資料來源與適用條件。在代表性水質與溫度下做時間序列試驗，保留材料批號及合規文件，將土倉與廢土處理需求一起審查；任何產品使用由專業團隊依現場核准方案決定，本課不提供化學配方。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for aging and environmental compatibility. Run time-series tests at representative temperature and water chemistry with batch and compliance records, reviewing chamber and spoil-treatment needs together; specialists select products under an approved site plan, without a chemical recipe from this course.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「老化與環境相容」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Aging and environmental compatibility\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","刀盤功率降低就能證明改良成功，不必看進尺和地質。","在代表性水質與溫度下做時間序列試驗，保留材料批號及合規文件，將土倉與廢土處理需求一起審查；任何產品使用由專業團隊依現場核准方案決定，本課不提供化學配方。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Lower cutterhead power proves successful conditioning without checking advance or geology.","Run time-series tests at representative temperature and water chemistry with batch and compliance records, reviewing chamber and spoil-treatment needs together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在代表性水質與溫度下做時間序列試驗，保留材料批號及合規文件，將土倉與廢土處理需求一起審查；任何產品使用由專業團隊依現場核准方案決定，本課不提供化學配方。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run time-series tests at representative temperature and water chemistry with batch and compliance records, reviewing chamber and spoil-treatment needs together; specialists select products under an approved site plan, without a chemical recipe from this course. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b136-v14-36","title":"老化與環境相容：失效診斷","titleEn":"Aging and environmental compatibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「老化與環境相容」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Aging and environmental compatibility” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"材料短期有效卻在停放後分離會使重啟困難，處理場又可能面臨不相容廢土；只記產品名稱而不記批次和水質，無法追查性能改變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Material that separates during rest complicates restart and can create incompatible spoil for treatment. Product names without batch and water-chemistry records cannot trace the reason for changed performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：材料短期有效卻在停放後分離會使重啟困難，處理場又可能面臨不相容廢土；只記產品名稱而不記批次和水質，無法追查性能改變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Product names without batch and water-chemistry records cannot trace the reason for changed performance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「材料短時試驗合格就保證任何溫度和停放時間都相容。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing a short trial guarantees compatibility at every temperature and storage duration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"材料短期有效卻在停放後分離會使重啟困難，處理場又可能面臨不相容廢土；只記產品名稱而不記批次和水質，無法追查性能改變。","textEn":"Material that separates during rest complicates restart and can create incompatible spoil for treatment. Product names without batch and water-chemistry records cannot trace the reason for changed performance.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「老化與環境相容」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Aging and environmental compatibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["材料短期有效卻在停放後分離會使重啟困難，處理場又可能面臨不相容廢土；只記產品名稱而不記批次和水質，無法追查性能改變。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只保留最成功配比試驗就足以說明改良方案適用範圍。"],"optionsEn":["Material that separates during rest complicates restart and can create incompatible spoil for treatment.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Retaining only the most successful trial fully describes the conditioning scheme's applicability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料短期有效卻在停放後分離會使重啟困難，處理場又可能面臨不相容廢土；只記產品名稱而不記批次和水質，無法追查性能改變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Material that separates during rest complicates restart and can create incompatible spoil for treatment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b136-v14-37","title":"改良試驗到現場移交：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Conditioning trials and field handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「改良試驗到現場移交」如何影響土壓平衡潛盾土壤改良的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Conditioning trials and field handover” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ground conditioning for EPB tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"小型試驗提供比較基礎，實際土倉有更大剪切、壓力與停留時間分布，尺度轉移須逐步驗證。交接應保留失敗組合及適用地層，不能只交最佳結果，讓下個班次知道何時原判斷不再成立。 假設12組試驗中8組符合預定雙重功能要求，比例66.7%；其餘4組仍需保留原因，不能刪除。 只挑成功試驗會掩蓋接近失效的邊界，跨地層仍沿用原方案則忽略材料變化；若沒有版本紀錄，性能異常時也無法判明採用哪一組假設。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「改良試驗到現場移交」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Small trials support comparisons, while a chamber has different shear, pressure and residence-time distributions. Scale transfer requires verification, including unsuccessful trials and applicable ground, so later shifts know when the original interpretation no longer holds. If 8 of an assumed 12 trials satisfy predefined dual-function requirements, the proportion is 66.7%; retain reasons for the other 4 rather than deleting them. Reporting only successful trials hides nearby failure boundaries, while transferring them across strata ignores changed material. Without version records, later anomalies cannot be linked to the assumptions actually in use. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Conditioning trials and field handover” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「只保留最成功配比試驗就足以說明改良方案適用範圍。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Retaining only the most successful trial fully describes the conditioning scheme's applicability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「改良試驗到現場移交」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Conditioning trials and field handover”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-37-k1","title":"改良試驗到現場移交","titleEn":"Conditioning trials and field handover","text":"小型試驗提供比較基礎，實際土倉有更大剪切、壓力與停留時間分布，尺度轉移須逐步驗證。交接應保留失敗組合及適用地層，不能只交最佳結果，讓下個班次知道何時原判斷不再成立。","textEn":"Small trials support comparisons, while a chamber has different shear, pressure and residence-time distributions. Scale transfer requires verification, including unsuccessful trials and applicable ground, so later shifts know when the original interpretation no longer holds.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只保留最成功配比試驗就足以說明改良方案適用範圍。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Retaining only the most successful trial fully describes the conditioning scheme's applicability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「改良試驗到現場移交」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Conditioning trials and field handover\" is correct?","options":["只保留最成功配比試驗就足以說明改良方案適用範圍。","小型試驗提供比較基礎，實際土倉有更大剪切、壓力與停留時間分布，尺度轉移須逐步驗證。","改良土越稀越容易流動，就一定越有利於穩定支護。"],"optionsEn":["Retaining only the most successful trial fully describes the conditioning scheme's applicability.","Small trials support comparisons, while a chamber has different shear, pressure and residence-time distributions.","More fluid conditioned soil is necessarily better for stable face support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"小型試驗提供比較基礎，實際土倉有更大剪切、壓力與停留時間分布，尺度轉移須逐步驗證。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Small trials support comparisons, while a chamber has different shear, pressure and residence-time distributions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b136-v14-38","title":"改良試驗到現場移交：定量估算","titleEn":"Conditioning trials and field handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「改良試驗到現場移交」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Conditioning trials and field handover” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設12組試驗中8組符合預定雙重功能要求，比例66.7%；其餘4組仍需保留原因，不能刪除。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If 8 of an assumed 12 trials satisfy predefined dual-function requirements, the proportion is 66.7%; retain reasons for the other 4 rather than deleting them. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：交付土樣來源、試驗邊界、量測原檔與地層適用表，現場再核對壓力、出土與沉陷三類證據；改變方案需經地工與設備負責人共同審查，不用學徒算例直接控制機器。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Deliver sample origin, boundaries, raw measurements and applicable ground, then cross-check pressure, discharge and movement in the field; changes require joint geotechnical and equipment review, not direct control from an apprentice calculation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設12組試驗中8組符合預定雙重功能要求，比例66.7%；其餘4組仍需保留原因，不能刪除。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If 8 of an assumed 12 trials satisfy predefined dual-function requirements, the proportion is 66.7%; retain reasons for the other 4 rather than deleting them.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「改良試驗到現場移交」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Conditioning trials and field handover\", which statement holds?","options":["常壓泡沫體積就是進入加壓土倉後的有效氣體體積。","單一剪切速率的黏度足以代表停放和重啟流變行為。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Atmospheric foam volume equals its effective gas volume inside the pressurized chamber.","Viscosity at one shear rate fully represents rest and restart rheology.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b136-v14-39","title":"改良試驗到現場移交：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Conditioning trials and field handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「改良試驗到現場移交」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Conditioning trials and field handover” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"交付土樣來源、試驗邊界、量測原檔與地層適用表，現場再核對壓力、出土與沉陷三類證據；改變方案需經地工與設備負責人共同審查，不用學徒算例直接控制機器。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只挑成功試驗會掩蓋接近失效的邊界，跨地層仍沿用原方案則忽略材料變化；若沒有版本紀錄，性能異常時也無法判明採用哪一組假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Deliver sample origin, boundaries, raw measurements and applicable ground, then cross-check pressure, discharge and movement in the field; changes require joint geotechnical and equipment review, not direct control from an apprentice calculation. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Reporting only successful trials hides nearby failure boundaries, while transferring them across strata ignores changed material. Without version records, later anomalies cannot be linked to the assumptions actually in use. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄改良試驗到現場移交的資料來源與適用條件。交付土樣來源、試驗邊界、量測原檔與地層適用表，現場再核對壓力、出土與沉陷三類證據；改變方案需經地工與設備負責人共同審查，不用學徒算例直接控制機器。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for conditioning trials and field handover. Deliver sample origin, boundaries, raw measurements and applicable ground, then cross-check pressure, discharge and movement in the field; changes require joint geotechnical and equipment review, not direct control from an apprentice calculation.","failure":"注意干擾：只挑成功試驗會掩蓋接近失效的邊界，跨地層仍沿用原方案則忽略材料變化；若沒有版本紀錄，性能異常時也無法判明採用哪一組假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reporting only successful trials hides nearby failure boundaries, while transferring them across strata ignores changed material. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"交付土樣來源、試驗邊界、量測原檔與地層適用表，現場再核對壓力、出土與沉陷三類證據；改變方案需經地工與設備負責人共同審查，不用學徒算例直接控制機器。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只挑成功試驗會掩蓋接近失效的邊界，跨地層仍沿用原方案則忽略材料變化；若沒有版本紀錄，性能異常時也無法判明採用哪一組假設。","textEn":"Deliver sample origin, boundaries, raw measurements and applicable ground, then cross-check pressure, discharge and movement in the field; changes require joint geotechnical and equipment review, not direct control from an apprentice calculation. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Reporting only successful trials hides nearby failure boundaries, while transferring them across strata ignores changed material. Without version records, later anomalies cannot be linked to the assumptions actually in use.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄改良試驗到現場移交的資料來源與適用條件。交付土樣來源、試驗邊界、量測原檔與地層適用表，現場再核對壓力、出土與沉陷三類證據；改變方案需經地工與設備負責人共同審查，不用學徒算例直接控制機器。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for conditioning trials and field handover. Deliver sample origin, boundaries, raw measurements and applicable ground, then cross-check pressure, discharge and movement in the field; changes require joint geotechnical and equipment review, not direct control from an apprentice calculation.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「改良試驗到現場移交」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Conditioning trials and field handover\"?","options":["交付土樣來源、試驗邊界、量測原檔與地層適用表，現場再核對壓力、出土與沉陷三類證據；改變方案需經地工與設備負責人共同審查，不用學徒算例直接控制機器。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","添加總量達標就證明各區材料分布一定均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Deliver sample origin, boundaries, raw measurements and applicable ground, then cross-check pressure, discharge and movement in the field.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Meeting the total addition quantity proves uniform distribution throughout the chamber."],"answer":0,"explanation":"交付土樣來源、試驗邊界、量測原檔與地層適用表，現場再核對壓力、出土與沉陷三類證據；改變方案需經地工與設備負責人共同審查，不用學徒算例直接控制機器。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Deliver sample origin, boundaries, raw measurements and applicable ground, then cross-check pressure, discharge and movement in the field; changes require joint geotechnical and equipment review, not direct control from an apprentice calculation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b136-v14-40","title":"改良試驗到現場移交：失效診斷","titleEn":"Conditioning trials and field handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b136-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「改良試驗到現場移交」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Conditioning trials and field handover” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只挑成功試驗會掩蓋接近失效的邊界，跨地層仍沿用原方案則忽略材料變化；若沒有版本紀錄，性能異常時也無法判明採用哪一組假設。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reporting only successful trials hides nearby failure boundaries, while transferring them across strata ignores changed material. Without version records, later anomalies cannot be linked to the assumptions actually in use. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只挑成功試驗會掩蓋接近失效的邊界，跨地層仍沿用原方案則忽略材料變化；若沒有版本紀錄，性能異常時也無法判明採用哪一組假設。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Without version records, later anomalies cannot be linked to the assumptions actually in use.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只保留最成功配比試驗就足以說明改良方案適用範圍。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Retaining only the most successful trial fully describes the conditioning scheme's applicability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b136-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只挑成功試驗會掩蓋接近失效的邊界，跨地層仍沿用原方案則忽略材料變化；若沒有版本紀錄，性能異常時也無法判明採用哪一組假設。","textEn":"Reporting only successful trials hides nearby failure boundaries, while transferring them across strata ignores changed material. Without version records, later anomalies cannot be linked to the assumptions actually in use.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b136-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「改良試驗到現場移交」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Conditioning trials and field handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只挑成功試驗會掩蓋接近失效的邊界，跨地層仍沿用原方案則忽略材料變化；若沒有版本紀錄，性能異常時也無法判明採用哪一組假設。","改良土越稀越容易流動，就一定越有利於穩定支護。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Reporting only successful trials hides nearby failure boundaries, while transferring them across strata ignores changed material.","More fluid conditioned soil is necessarily better for stable face support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只挑成功試驗會掩蓋接近失效的邊界，跨地層仍沿用原方案則忽略材料變化；若沒有版本紀錄，性能異常時也無法判明採用哪一組假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reporting only successful trials hides nearby failure boundaries, while transferring them across strata ignores changed material. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-herrenknecht-epb","v14s-geo","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
